        <p>‘Ad<expan>r</expan>ae <expan>búaid</expan> ⁊ <expan>bennachtain</expan> a anu<expan>m</expan>, a <name type="person" nymRef="C6"><expan>Chaīlti</expan></name>’, a<expan>r</expan> <name type="person" nymRef="D25">Dīa<expan>r</expan>maid m<expan>ac</expan> Cerbaill</name>, ‘⁊ cāit a fuil<expan>et</expan> sin ⁊ senchaidi fer <name type="place" nymRef="e6">nÉr<expan>end</expan></name>? Scrībt<expan>ar</expan> lib i tā<expan>m</expan>lorgaib fil<expan>ed</expan> ⁊ i <expan>m</expan>b<expan>r</expan>īathraib oll<expan>am</expan>an sūd ⁊ b<expan>er</expan>ed cách a <expan>cu</expan>id leis dā c<expan>r</expan>īch ⁊ dā ferand fēi<expan>n</expan> dē’.</p>
        <p>⁊ do sc<expan>r</expan>īb<expan>ad</expan> oca n-ugda<expan>r</expan>aib ⁊ oca fil<expan>ed</expan>aib ⁊ oca n-oll<expan>am</expan>naib i<expan>n</expan> scélaighe<expan>cht</expan> si<expan>n</expan> ⁊ ruc cách a cuid cu<expan>m</expan> a c<expan>r</expan>īchi ⁊ a cōigid leis dī.</p>
        
        
